This is a long kit. At about 70% context start no new part; at about 75% stop at a safe boundary (a commit made or not started, files whole, every process you started stopped by pid, the bands free, the lock released or your ticket named) and write `/Volumes/Datasec_DEV/!CODING/Datasec/NexusAI/1_Project_Definition/Briefs/2026-11-27_B2175_HANDOVER.md` (done / in hand / next / processes left / decisions a successor keeps) with last line `HANDOVER B2175: next <part> <step> | done <parts>`, and end STATUS with the same line. Parts: read, tickets, trees, pair-base, edit, pair-head, cell-control, update, plain, push, lock-copies, baseline, build, regression, slot-arms, mutants, install-dry. **Size (PREDICTED):** reading, clone and `npm ci` about 30 min; the three rd490 runs a few minutes each (UNMEASURED alone); the two whole-suite runs about 25 min each; Part L about 2 h (the arms twice, your candidate, slot arms and mutants); plus any queue wait. If the band is reached before P10, nothing is pushed (HARD STOP); after P10, Part L hands over.

## STOP RULES (each `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <one question>`)
Any REFUSE condition; main moved by a path HOLD 20 does not allow; the branch exists at origin; a blob or frozen sha not as stated; P2 not red-first; P4 not `OWN-SLOTS-DISJOINT` and `BOTH-GREEN`; P5 not exactly the new cell red; a verify not `VERDICT: PASS` or a pair not 6635 / 419; a red cell other than those named (name it; one rerun in a NEW acquisition only if every failure names a 429, `EADDRINUSE` or a boot timeout, said so in STATUS; two in a row: STOP); an arm red on the live copy (L1); a slot arm red on the candidate, or a control arm green on the live copy where this kit says FAIL; a mutant that no arm catches; the live script's sha256 or inode changing at any time; a Jira create that cannot be confirmed by search; jest outside the live lock or with `NODE_OPTIONS` set or in a tree with a dot-segment; a need to touch a path outside OWNS-B2175. **HARD STOP** (slot): push nothing unproven; committed but unpushed work is `CODED-UNPROVEN b2175/rd490-portband <sha40>` with the steps that ran; write the HANDOVER.

## STATUS FILE (the channel)
`/Volumes/Datasec_DEV/!CODING/Datasec/NexusAI/1_Project_Definition/Briefs/2026-11-27_B2175_STATUS.md`. First line `B2175 STATUS (placeholder, Step 0 running)`. Sections: Questions, BLUF, Step 0, Step 1, Tickets, PRIOR WORK, Trees, Pair, Commits, Verify, Lock, `## READY`, ADDENDA READ, NOT TESTED, Corrections. **The LAST line on finish is exactly one of:** `READY B2175: <K sha40> | candidate <sha256>`, or `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <one question>`, or the HANDOVER line. In between: `WORKING: ...`. Poll `ls /Volumes/Datasec_DEV/TUESDAY/2_Project_Files/tuesday/briefs/ | /usr/bin/grep -i -E '^2026-11-2[789]_B2175_(ADDENDUM|ANSWER)'` at every step boundary (control: the same grep with `SEAT-N186` prints this kit, its sidecar and any `.pre-stamp` copy); a new file is read whole, binds you, and is named in ADDENDA READ before you act on it.

## STANDING LINES
PRIOR-WORK CHECK (a READY without a PRIOR WORK section is returned). No deploy, no PR, no merge to main, Jira only as Step 2 says, no mail, no message to any human. Never delete (quarantine). Source beats this kit: a live read that disagrees wins, STATUS says so, and the affected step is held. Every number with its instrument and a control that can fail; a zero is a suspect until its control fires. Any step that rewrites a file builds and encodes the whole new content first, writes it to a temp file beside the target, then `os.replace`s it. You never write that the product owner chose anything in committed text, Jira text or STATUS: every choice here is the coordinator's default.

